    "short_description": "The United States Air Force (USAF) is the aerial and space warfare branch of the U.S. Armed Forces, established as an independent service in 1947. Its mission is to \"Fly, Fight, and Win…airpower anytime, anywhere,\" guided by core values of integrity, service, and excellence. The USAF plays a crucial role in defending the United States through airpower, maintaining air superiority, strategic deterrence, and global strike capabilities.\n\nThe USAF has a rich history, evolving from early aviation efforts in the early 20th century to a major military force involved in significant conflicts such as World War I, World War II, the Korean War, and the Gulf War. Its core roles include air combat, strategic attack, logistical support, and defense integration, ensuring effective operations in joint missions with other military branches. The USAF also focuses on training and support for its personnel, ensuring readiness and capability across its various commands.",
